cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the EOLA Research Toolkit in research, please cite the
  software release and the associated dataset.

title: "EOLA Research Toolkit"
type: software
version: "2.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23218886"
license: "BSD-3-Clause"

authors:
  - family-names: "Hechavarria-Hernandez"
    given-names: "Jesus Rafael"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9013-8665"

abstract: >-
  The EOLA Research Toolkit is a reproducible computational framework
  for fairness-aware and explainable student-risk modeling in online
  higher education. It provides canonical dataset acquisition and
  integrity verification, exact reproduction of published baseline
  experiments, 30-seed robust predictive and subgroup-fairness
  evaluation, threshold and Pareto sensitivity analysis, and
  explanation-level disparity analysis using GEDI and Weighted GEDI.
  The toolkit represents the scientific and reproducibility layer only
  and is not an institutional production decision system.

keywords:
  - learning analytics
  - fairness-aware machine learning
  - explainable artificial intelligence
  - higher education
  - student risk
  - reproducible research
  - SHAP
  - equalized odds
  - GEDI
  - responsible AI

references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "ECOTEC_Online Student Risk Dataset"
    version: "v1.0.4"
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22015963"

repository-code: "https://github.com/jrhechavarriah/EOLA-Research-Toolkit"